- At 744 the sidebar is 232 px, so 210 px inside.
- `workshop.css`'s `@media (max-width: 760px)` block puts the label beside the select and sets the select to 16 px. The select is then about 104 px wide, against 178.5 px of text.
- Stacking the label alone is not enough. 16 px text needs a select about 218 px wide (it is cut at 214), and only 210 px is available.
- At 13 px, the body size and what 820 already uses, the text is 145 px and fits with room to spare.
- A native select's `scrollWidth` never reports clipped text, so the check must measure the text itself.

