# Plan (sonnet, medium)

**Goal.** At 744×1133 the deck builder's "Compare with" picker shows its label and its chosen option ("Another deck or a trio…") in full, and the editor has no horizontal overflow. The layouts at 820×1180, 390×844 and the desktop sizes are unchanged. A spec 46 check fails on the clipped picker. The fix is CSS only, plus the proof and a ruling note.

**Cause (measured in headless Chromium with the shipped Inter font).**
- At 744 the sidebar is 232 px, so 210 px inside.
- `workshop.css`'s `@media (max-width: 760px)` block puts the label beside the select and sets the select to 16 px. The select is then about 104 px wide, against 178.5 px of text.
- Stacking the label alone is not enough. 16 px text needs a select about 218 px wide (it is cut at 214), and only 210 px is available.
- At 13 px, the body size and what 820 already uses, the text is 145 px and fits with room to spare.
- A native select's `scrollWidth` never reports clipped text, so the check must measure the text itself.

## Files to touch

| File | | What changes |
|---|---|---|
| `apps/web/src/game/deckbuilder/workshop.css` | change | One new `@media` block after the `(max-width: 760px)` block |
| `apps/web/src/game/deckbuilder/layout.test.ts` | change | New `describe`/`it` named `R4349000 …` that reads the sheet |
| `e2e/cypress/e2e/46-menus-fit-one-screen.cy.ts` | change | Imports, constant `SELECT_ARROW_PX`, helper `expectComparePickerWhole`, new `it("R4349000 …")` |
| `spec/rulings/R4349000.md` | new | The ruling note (amends R3956000) |
| `spec/pending/4349.md` | new | The §11 paragraph |

- **Do not touch:** `DeckEditor.tsx` (no markup change is needed), `.github/`, `.harness/`, `.squishy/`, `bot/`, `spec/11-rulings.md`, `spec/INDEX.md`, `spec/CARDS.md`, and any crate. Never run `cargo jackioh spec index`.
- **Governing notes:** [[R3956000]] (the 744 split and the 232 px sidebar), [[R3734001]], §9.4. CLAUDE.md rules 3 and 7 apply: this is presentation only.
- Issue #4349 owns R4349000–R4349999, so its first ruling is R4349000. `spec/rulings/` has none of them yet.

## Steps

1. **`workshop.css`: add the block.**
   - Put it right after the `@media (max-width: 760px) { … }` block that ends with the `/* 16 px keeps a phone from zooming … */` rule, and before the `/* A phone (the one-column editor, R3956000) … */` comment.
   - It must come after the 760 block: `.ws-compare-pick` has the same specificity there, so the later rule wins.
   - Use exactly this media query. Its three features are all named breakpoints, so `breakpoints.test.ts` stays green:
   ```css
   /* #4349 (R4349000): an iPad mini held upright (744 px) leaves the picker 210 px, where "Compare with" beside a
      16 px select cut "Another deck or a trio…" to a few letters, and that text needs 218 px even alone. From 601
      to 760 px, on a screen taller than a phone on its side, the label sits over the select (as from 761 px) and
      the select takes the body's 13 px (as at 820 px). A phone on its side keeps the row and its 16 px, which
      stops a phone zooming into the field. */
   @media (min-width: 601px) and (max-width: 760px) and (min-height: 501px) {
     .ws-compare-pick {
       flex-direction: column;
       align-items: stretch;
       gap: 3px;
     }

     .ws-compare-pick .ws-select {
       font-size: var(--type-md);
     }
   }
   ```
   - Do not edit the existing 760 block. Phones (600 px and under), 761 px and over, and phones on their side (500 px tall or less) keep today's rules.

2. **`layout.test.ts`: add a `describe("R4349000 the deck editor's Compare with picker", …)` at the end of the file.**
   - Copy the style of the `R3956000` tests: the file already has the `sheet()` and `rule()` helpers.
   - Add one `it("R4349000 from 601 to 760 px on a tall screen the label sits over the select, which takes the body's size", …)`:
   ```ts
   const workshop = sheet("game/deckbuilder/workshop.css");
   const narrow = workshop.indexOf("@media (max-width: 760px) {");
   expect(narrow, "the 760 px block").toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(0);
   const tall = workshop.indexOf("@media (min-width: 601px) and (max-width: 760px) and (min-height: 501px) {");
   expect(tall, "a block from 601 to 760 px on a tall screen").toBeGreaterThan(narrow);
   const pick = rule(workshop, ".ws-compare-pick", tall);
   expect(pick).toContain("flex-direction: column;");
   expect(pick).toContain("align-items: stretch;");
   expect(rule(workshop, ".ws-compare-pick .ws-select", tall)).toContain("font-size: var(--type-md);");
   // The phone's row and its 16 px stay in the 760 px block.
   expect(rule(workshop, ".ws-compare-pick", narrow)).toContain("flex-direction: row;");
   expect(rule(workshop, ".ws-compare-pick .ws-select", narrow)).toContain("flex: 1 1 auto;");
